2	//! groups and pattern modifiers) for lumen, reproducing the original runtime's behaviour.
3	//!
4	//! # API
5	//!
6	//! * [`parse_flags`] — flags string -> [`RegexFlags`]; `Err` is the exact SyntaxError text.
7	//! * [`compile`] — pattern (UTF-16) + flags -> [`CompiledRegex`] (cheap `Rc` clone); `Err` is
8	//!   the exact SyntaxError text. The same texts are used for regex *literals*: the original
9	//!   reports them as early errors when the script is parsed (`Uncaught SyntaxError: nothing to
10	//!   repeat`; inside `eval`/`Function` they are thrown as SyntaxError with the same message).
11	//!   Only the lexer-level `/[/` case differs: "unterminated regular expression".
12	//! * [`CompiledRegex::exec`] — RegExpBuiltinExec core: `exec(input, last_index)` searches from
13	//!   `last_index` (only *at* it when sticky) and returns UTF-16 spans for groups
14	//!   `0..=capture_count()`, `None` for non-participating groups. In u/v mode a `last_index`
15	//!   pointing at the low half of a surrogate pair starts the attempt at the pair (the original
16	//!   reports `index` = pair start, e.g. `/./gu` with lastIndex 1 on "😀" gives index 0,
17	//!   lastIndex 2). `last_index > len` -> `None`. The JS layer handles lastIndex itself:
18	//!   pass 0 when neither `g` nor `y`.
19	//! * [`CompiledRegex::group_names`] (or the borrowing `group_names_ref`) — named groups in
20	//!   source order, each with all its group indices (duplicate names in different
21	//!   alternatives). `groups.name` is the value of the first participating index (or
22	//!   undefined); property order = first occurrence order. `capture_count()`, `flags()`,
23	//!   `has_named_groups()` are also available.
24	//! * [`escape_source`] — `RegExp.prototype.source` text: "" -> `(?:)`; `/` outside classes
25	//!   -> `\/` (kept raw inside `[...]`, an already escaped `\/` is kept); LF/CR/U+2028/U+2029
26	//!   -> `\n` `\r` ` ` ` ` (also when escaped: `\<LF>` -> `\n`); tabs etc. raw.
27	//! * [`RegexFlags::to_flags_string`] — the `flags` getter order "dgimsuvy".
28	//!
29	//! # Error messages (SyntaxError `message`, no prefix)
30	//!
31	//! Flags (scanned left to right, u+v checked last): `invalid regular expression flag X`,
32	//! `duplicate regular expression flag X`, `the u and v regular expression flags are mutually
33	//! exclusive` (X = the character; the original keeps lone surrogates raw, we emit U+FFFD).
34	//!
35	//! Pattern (first error in a left-to-right parse; then, after a successful parse: unknown
